2. **Projection onto the \( xy \)-Plane**:
   - The projection \( P_2(x) \) will retain only the first two components \( x_1 \) and \( x_2 \), effectively projecting \( x \) onto the \( xy \)-plane.
   - Mathematically, \( P_2(x) = (x_1, x_2, 0) \).

